    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Academic-Advisor_JR100759": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Academic Advisor ‌ Xavier University’s Office of Academic Advising and Learning Support (OALS) is seeking an Academic Advisor with specific focus on first-year and at-risk student population. This position serves as a professional academic advisor and collaborates with faculty and staff to help undergraduate students meet their academic and co-curricular goals. The Academic Advisor assists students in understanding major and core requirements, planning satisfactory academic progress, course selection and registration.  This position provides targeted support and outreach to students on academic probation and those identified as needing additional academic support and coaching.  In addition, this role collaborates with colleagues on communication, evaluation, and assessment efforts for OALS. OALS equips students to confidently navigate their educational journey through personalized academic advising and comprehensive learning support. We partner with each student to identify and reflect on their unique goals and develop a clear path to graduation. We consult with faculty advisors as they work to support advisees and academically struggling students. Together, we strive to ensure that every student feels supported, valued, and informed, takes responsibility for their academic progress, and realizes their educational goals. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide individualized, developmental, appreciative academic advising to 200+ current and prospective undergraduate students with specific emphasis on first-year and at-risk students. Provide academic support to at-risk and probationary undergraduate students in the assigned caseload. Contribute to the development and implementation of common outreach campaigns and assessment efforts. Collaborate with Faculty Advisors, Academic Departments, Career Development, Care and Support, Admissions, Financial Aid, Student Life, Thrive, and other offices across Xavier University. JOB REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor’s degree required in related field; Master’s degree preferred 1-3 years of relevant experience Intermediate communication skills, analytical skills, project/process management skills, computer/technical skills, and office administrative support skills To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University's website. Applications will be reviewed immediately and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.  Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Adjunct-Faculty--Department-of-Music---Theatre_JR100550": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Music & Theatre",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Adjunct Faculty, Department of Music & Theatre ‌ Xavier University is seeking qualified candidates to join our pool of potential adjunct faculty for the 2026-2027 academic year. This posting is intended to collect applications for part-time, non-tenure-track position for an Adjunct Instructor in the Department of Music & Theatre. Candidates must be dedicated to undergraduate teaching and demonstrate excellence in their field.   The successful candidate(s) will contribute to our commitment to excellence in teaching and student engagement. Applications will be accepted on a continuous basis , and candidates may be contacted as teaching needs arise. Adjunct faculty contracts are issued on a semester-by-semester basis , depending on departmental needs and student enrollment. Minimum Qualifications: Candidates may qualify with a master’s degree in a related field accompanied by significant professional experience or a relevant graduate degree. Demonstrated ability to teach at the college level. Ability and experience to teach one or more of the following courses in the department: o    Music in Film (MUSC 106) o    Private Lesson: Voice (MUSC 282) o    Private Lesson: Electric Guitar (MUSC 283) o    Private Lesson: Drum Set (MUSC 298) o    Private Lesson: Jazz Piano (MUSC 298) o    Voice and Movement for the Actor (THTR 121) o    Voice for Theatre Majors (THTR 197) o    Lighting Design (THTR 331) o    Jazz Dance I (DANC 155) o    Musical Theatre Dance (DANC 201) o    Trumpet (MUSC 294) Duties include: Teach assigned course(s). Effective planning and preparation of lectures, discussions, and activities to support student success. Use Xavier’s campus-wide academic program, Canvas, to provide course information and maintain an electronic record of student’s progress. Working cooperatively with members of the department.   For additional information, please contact Stephen Skiles, Chair, Department of Music & Theatre at skiless1@xavier.edu . To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University’s website.   Please note: This adjunct faculty pool will close on May 1, 2027 . If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new adjunct pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is an equal opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Service-Desk-Technician-I_JR100453": {
      "title": "Service Desk Technician I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Service Desk Technician I ‌ Xavier currently seeks to hire a Service Desk Technician. The Service Desk Technician works within the Information Technologies division to provide consistent, quality Tier I/II technical support to the Xavier campus community. This includes responding effectively to myriad technical issues and requests made to the Service Desk via email, phone, walkup and self-service. This position also provides mentoring to Xavier’s student helpdesk technicians.  The hours for this position are 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday through Friday. Xavier University is seeking a dedicated and mission-driven Service Desk Technician to join our IT team. This role presents an exciting opportunity for an individual who thrives in a collaborative, student-focused environment and is passionate about contributing to work that makes a meaningful impact. At Xavier, our mission is to educate the whole person—intellectually, morally, and spiritually—in the Jesuit tradition. The Service Desk Technician plays a vital part in advancing this mission by working within the Information Technologies division to provide consistent, quality Tier I/II technical support to the Xavier campus community. This includes responding effectively to myriad technical issues and requests made to the Service Desk via email, phone, walkup and self-service. This position also provides mentoring to Xavier’s student helpdesk technicians. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to shape initiatives, strengthen campus services, and help create a community where all members can learn, grow, and succeed.  JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide first level contact, follow-ups, and resolutions to customer issues. Ensure accurate incident recording, documentation and prompt closure of tickets. Escalate tickets to an appropriate area or operating unit, as warranted. Author internal and public knowledge base articles for documentation and how-to purposes. Perform (re)imaging of PCs, migration of user data, and minor desktop/laptop hardware replacement. Interact with appropriate vendors as needed to resolve advanced issues. Additional duties as assigned. JOB REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related degree with 1+ year of experience in an IT support role; or an Associate’s degree with 3+ years of experience in an IT support role. Proficiency working with and troubleshooting Windows and Mac operating systems, printers, peripherals, mobile devices (iOS and Android) Proficiency working with and troubleshooting Office 365. Ability to perform basic PC hardware troubleshooting, imaging and data migration. Experience with ITSM/ticketing software, TeamDynamix prefered. Excellent customer service and problem-solving skills. Excellent oral/written communication skills. Ability to thrive as part of a team as well as work independently. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience in a higher education environment. Experience providing remote support (SCCM, Bomgar, Teams etc.) CompTIA A+ certification. To ensure consideration, interested applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University's website.  Review of applications will start on August 3, 2026 and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.  Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Human-Resources-Coordinator_JR100659": {
      "title": "Human Resources Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Human Resources Coordinator ‌ Xavier University’s Office of Human Resources is seeking a welcoming, dependable, and detail-oriented Human Resources Coordinator who can manage multiple responsibilities while making a positive first impression on everyone who enters or contacts the Office of Human Resources.  Reporting to the Executive Assistant of Human Resources, this role provides exceptional customer service, manages front desk operations, answers phone calls, and performs a variety of administrative tasks to support the office's daily operations, including various projects for the Vice President and Chief Human Resources Officer and members of the Human Resources team.  This position handles confidential information and fields various inquiries received from constituents both on and off campus.          The ideal candidate must be well-organized, excellent at multitasking, and able to function both independently and collaboratively with other members of the Office of Human Resources and constituents across campus. The individual will exercise a high level of confidentiality, attention to detail, and a dedication to excellence in their work.   Main Responsibilities: Serves as the first point of contact for the Office of Human Resources. Greets and welcomes visitors in a courteous and professional manner. Responds to internal and external inquiries either in-person, by phone, or via the Human Resources office inbox, exercising sound judgement in determining which inquiries can be resolved independently and which require escalation to the appropriate HR team member. Maintain a clean, organized, and professional reception area. Understand basic HR functions and navigation of the Workday system. Assist with filing, data entry, copying, scanning, and document preparation. Maintain office supplies, inventory, and organization of office resources. Understand and interpret HR processes, practices, and policies. Receive, open, and distribute daily mail, packages, and correspondence to appropriate team members. Support the Vice President and Chief Human Resources Officer and members of the team with various administrative tasks and special projects. Provide administrative support for onboarding of student employees in Workday and processing of student employment records, ensuring accuracy and compliance with policies and procedures. Assist members of the HR team with onboarding of new hires, including I-9 completion and gathering of new hire paperwork.  Assist with setup and support of departmental meetings and events. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent required. Bachelor’s degree preferred. 3 – 5 years of relevant experience. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, and Outlook) Previous experience with Workday is a plus. Excellent written and interpersonal, analytical, and office/administrative support skills. Basic project and process management skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and responsibilities. Strong organizational and multitasking abilities. Professional approach and positive attitude. Embraces Xavier’s Jesuit Catholic identity and Ignatian values. Handles confidential information with professionalism, integrity, and discretion. To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University's website. Review of applications will start on August 10, 2026, and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion. Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Athletics-Ticketing-Coordinator_JR100316": {
      "title": "Athletics Ticketing Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Athletics Ticketing Coordinator ‌ Xavier University, a member of the BIG EAST Conference, seeks qualified candidates for the position of Ticketing Coordinator, which will serve an integral role in the operations of the ticket department. This is an hourly position and will focus on the management and execution of ticket operational tasks such as training of student workers, scheduling workers for all events, processing of orders and other general office tasks as needed.  Other duties will include assisting the department with gameday box office support, coordinating sales and service for customers, e-mail communications, and collaborating and supporting other department initiatives including fundraising and hospitality efforts. The position will be required to work in the office as well as at athletic events. Qualifications include: 1+ year of experience in a collegiate ticket department or related field Professional, results-oriented self-starter who takes initiative to solve problems Excellent verbal and written communication skills Ability to meet deadlines and prioritize multiple responsibilities Strong organizational skills Proficient in Microsoft Office suite Proficiency with Paciolan ticketing and Eloqua marketing automation systems is preferred Bachelor’s degree in marketing, sports management or a related field is preferred Employment Term Start Date: Beginning no earlier than August 1, 2026. This is a 10-month position for 1 year with the mutual option for a possible 2nd year. Evening, weekend and holiday hours will be required and schedule may vary. There are no benefits attached to this position. This position will work no more than 25 hours per week from August through May.  Compensation Hourly rate of $15/hour. To ensure consideration, interested applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University's website.  Review of applications will start on August 3, 2026 and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.  Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Maintenance-Technician_JR100594": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Maintenance Technician ‌ Xavier University’s Office of Physical Plant is seeking applications for the role of Maintenance Technician. This position plays a key role in maintaining a safe, functional, and comfortable campus environment. The ideal candidate will be a well-rounded technician! with hands-on experience in multiple trades and a proactive mindset toward preventive maintenance and timely repairs. The Maintenance Technician performs general maintenance tasks across a variety of building systems, including plumbing, electrical, HVAC, and other mechanical components. This position supports the upkeep of campus facilities through routine preventive maintenance, prompt response to work orders, and collaboration with other skilled trades. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: • Troubleshoot and repair plumbing, electrical, HVAC, and mechanical systems. • Perform preventive maintenance on building systems and equipment. • Complete and manage work orders through the campus CMMS system. • Prioritize tasks to ensure safety and minimize downtime. • Work both independently and as part of a team to support university operations. • Follow all safety guidelines and standard operating procedures. • Availability to be on-call on a rotational schedule.  Required Qualifications: • High school diploma or GED required; vocational or technical training preferred. • 3–5 years of experience in a facilities or maintenance-related role. • Valid driver’s license with an insurable driving record. • Demonstrated mechanical aptitude and proficiency with standard tools. • Ability to lift and move heavy equipment (up to 50 lbs.), and work from ladders or in confined spaces. • Strong communication skills and the ability to interact with various departments and stakeholders. Working Conditions: • Work is performed both indoors and outdoors in varying weather conditions. • Exposure to noise, vibrations, chemicals, and confined spaces is common. • Must be comfortable performing physically demanding tasks including bending, stooping, crawling, kneeling, and climbing. To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University's website. Review of applications will start on July 27, 2026 and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion. Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. ‌ HVAC Certified / Licensed Electrician? Apply today, your credentials are a strong plus for this role. We want to talk to you! Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Director-of-Adult-Education_JR100563": {
      "title": "Director of Adult Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Director of Adult Education ‌ Xavier University invites applications for the position of Director of Adult Education, a strategic leadership role dedicated to supporting the important demographic of adult undergraduate learners at Xavier, expanding opportunities for them, and strengthening pathways to degree completion. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Arts & Sciences, the Director of Adult Education will provide institution-wide leadership for adult learner initiatives, working collaboratively across Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, and Xavier's academic colleges. The successful candidate will offer vision in shaping and implementing strategies that support adult student recruitment, enrollment, retention, and graduation, all grounded in Xavier University's mission of educational excellence and student success. Additionally, the successful candidate will use data-informed decision making and market insights to enhance the adult learner experience from initial inquiry through degree completion. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE: Strategic Leadership: Lead the development and implementation of Xavier University's vision and strategy for adult undergraduate education and identify academic pathways, degree-completion programs, and certificate opportunities aligned with adult student needs. Student Success and Support: Coordinate university-wide efforts to support adult learners throughout the student lifecycle, in collaboration with advising, financial aid, enrollment, student affairs, and academic units to ensure a seamless student experience. Academic Operations: Coordinate adult education initiatives across academic and administrative units and collaborate with faculty and college leadership to align course offerings and academic pathways with student demand. Assessment and Continuous Improvement: Analyze enrollment, retention, and completion data for adult learners, develop recommendations that inform strategic planning and decision-making, and support institutional assessment efforts and continuous improvement initiatives. Existing Programs: Provide oversight (for example, for curricular changes and degree sign-offs) and serve as key point of contact for Xavier’s current two undergraduate online degree programs (Bachelor of Liberal Arts and Bachelor of Arts in Organizational Leadership) and two certificate programs that are housed in the College of Arts & Sciences. JOB REQUIREMENTS: Master’s degree in Higher Education or related field Five to ten years of relevant experience Excellent customer service skills Ability to master and organize details Ability to work both independently and collaboratively Ability to prioritize tasks to manage multiple projects Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging .  We strongly believe that our people make all the difference in cultivating an inclusive environment that welcomes ideas, encourages innovation, and manifests belonging. We welcome candidates from all walks of life with different strengths, experiences, beliefs, and backgrounds to apply. To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University's website.  Review of applications will start on July 27, 2026 and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion. Questions may be sent to CAS Associate Dean Stephen Yandell at  yandell@xavier.edu . ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Substitute-Teacher--St-Peter-Faber-Academy_JR100564": {
      "title": "Substitute Teacher, St. Peter Faber Academy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Substitute Teacher, St. Peter Faber Academy ‌ Xavier University is seeking qualified candidates to join our pool of potential St. Peter Faber Academy Substitute Teachers for the 2025-2026 academic year. This posting is intended to collect applications for  part-time substitute teachers to provide support in Preschool – 4th grade. St. Peter Faber Academy’s vision is to provide an innovative, holistic education where young minds are nurtured to become compassionate leaders, critical thinkers, and lifelong learners. Grounded in the Jesuit Catholic tradition, we cultivate every student’s unique potential through personalized education, academic rigor, and spiritual growth. Our students emerge as well-rounded individuals prepared to shape a just and sustainable world, embodying the values of reflection, discernment, and service. Applications will be  accepted on a continuous basis,  and candidates may be contacted as teaching needs arise. Qualifications: ·         Bachelor’s degree required ·         Valid Standard Ohio Teaching License (P-5 and/or 4-9) preferred For additional information, please contact Sarah Bitzer, Principal, St. Peter Faber Academy at  bitzers@xavier.edu . To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University’s website.  Please note:  This substitute teacher pool will  close on May 01, 2027 . If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new substitute pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is an equal opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Seasonal-Groundskeeper_JR100548": {
      "title": "Seasonal Groundskeeper",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Seasonal Groundskeeper ‌ Xavier University is seeking qualified candidates for a part‑time, Seasonal Groundskeeper, working 40 hours a week, for an employment period from April 2026 through October 2026. This posting is intended to identify applicants interested in contributing to Xavier’s mission during a defined seasonal period in support of campus needs. Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis, and candidates may be contacted as needs arise for the April–October 2026 season. Seasonal employment is based on project timelines, departmental priorities, and available funding, and is limited to the duration of the 2026 seasonal period. Responsibilities includes but not limited to: With appropriate personal protective equipment, the Temporary Groundskeeper will operate hand and power tools to cut, trim, edge grass, turf, prunes trees and shrubs, trim hedges, mulches, pulls weeds, and applies chemicals.  Maintain athletic fields by dragging, laying out, lining and painting. Keep university grounds clean (e.g., pick up papers and other debris; operates a variety of equipment to clean sidewalks, steps, patios, and parking lots when necessary). Follow all established safety procedures. Work outside in all-weather condition; work with potentially dangerous equipment and chemicals; exposed to dirt, dust, fumes, noise, and elements. To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a resume and cover letter on Xavier University’s website.   Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. Please note: This seasonal groundskeeer pool will close on September 1, 2026 . If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new seasonal groundskeeper pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
