    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Director--Territory-Recruitment_JR100518": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Territory Recruitment",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Director, Territory Recruitment ‌ Xavier University is seeking a dynamic and enthusiastic Assistant Director of Territory Recruitment to join our team! In this role, you'll be instrumental in guiding prospective students and their families through the admissions process, acting as a primary point of contact and an ambassador for Xavier. We're looking for someone with a strong aptitude for sales—someone who can effectively communicate the value of our academic programs and campus experience, addressing concerns and inspiring confidence. Exceptional customer service skills are paramount, as you'll build relationships and provide personalized support to a diverse range of individuals. The position also requires travel for recruitment events, so a willingness to hit the road and connect with future students is essential. This position is available as an on-campus role for candidates within the Cincinnati region, or as a remote opportunity for qualified applicants located in neighboring cities, including Columbus, Indianapolis, and Louisville. At least 1 year of relevant experience is required. If you're a highly motivated individual with a passion for education and a knack for connecting with people, we encourage you to apply! JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: Travel throughout assigned territory. Build relationships with high school students, their families, and high school guidance staff. Represent Xavier University in a positive manner. Organize and attend recruitment activities in assigned territory, such as college fairs, high school visits, etc. Evaluate applications for admission. Utilize CRM (Slate) to effectively monitor student and territory performance. JOB REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor’s degree required. At least 1 year in a similar role with comparable goals and responsibilities. Ability to adapt to a changing environment and handle multiple priorities. Excellent presentation, writing and analytical skills. Qualified candidates residing in the Greater Cincinnati area will serve in an on-campus capacity, while those located in neighboring regional areas may be eligible for a remote work arrangement. To ensure consideration, interested applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University's website.  Review of applications will start on July 1 , 2026 and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.  Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Professor-of-Instruction--College-of-Nursing_JR100503": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction, College of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Professor of Instruction, College of Nursing ‌ The College of Nursing (CN) at Xavier University is seeking an experienced, innovative, and highly motivated candidate for a full-time, nontenure-track faculty position (Assistant Professor of Instruction) to teach in our undergraduate and graduate nursing programs. The CN programs include BSN, second-degree accelerated MSN (MIDAS), MSN Education, Forensics, FNP, PMHNP, AGPCNP, and DNP programs, as well as a variety of post-master’s certificates. The successful candidate will teach across undergraduate and graduate programs.  Desired specialty areas include pediatrics and MSN core courses. Candidates with expertise in more than one specialty area are highly desirable. Candidates may teach in on-ground courses as well as in our online MSN and/or DNP graduate programs, depending on relevant academic preparation. The successful candidate will actively participate in the development and evaluation of curriculum, course content, clinical experiences, test construction, and assessment of students’ learning; establish effective coordinating relationships with co-workers and clinical agencies; participate in nursing scholarly work and professional development; participate in student academic advising and guidance; and participate in appropriate program, college, and university activities and committees. QUALIFICATIONS: Current and unencumbered license to practice as a registered nurse in Ohio or be eligible to be licensed and practice in Ohio. A doctoral degree in nursing or a related field is required for teaching in the graduate programs At least 2 years of clinical experience as a registered nurse in a specialty area (pediatrics preferred). At least 2 years of teaching experience in an accredited program in a content-specialty area is preferred. Teaching experience in online instruction is desired. Knowledge of curriculum development, methods of teaching, and evaluation are desired. Candidates must demonstrate excellent communication skills and have a strong commitment to working as part of a collaborative team. To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter, resume and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University's website.  Applications will be reviewed immediately and accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Adjunct-Faculty---College-of-Arts-and-Sciences_JR100323": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - College of Arts and Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Adjunct Faculty - College of Arts and Sciences ‌ Xavier University is seeking qualified candidates to join our pool of potential adjunct faculty for Fall 2026. This posting is intended to collect applications for part-time, non-tenure-track position for an Adjunct Instructor in the College of Arts and Sciences . Candidates must be dedicated to graduate or undergraduate teaching and demonstrate excellence in their field.   The successful candidate will contribute to our commitment to excellence in teaching and student engagement. Applications will be accepted on a continuous basis , and candidates may be contacted as teaching needs arise. Adjunct faculty contracts are issued on a semester-by-semester basis , depending on departmental needs and student enrollment. Minimum Qualifications: ·          Depending on the courses assigned, candidates may qualify with a master’s degree in a related field accompanied by significant professional experience or a relevant graduate degree. ·          Demonstrated ability to teach at the college level. Duties include: ·          Teach assigned course(s). ·          Effective planning and preparation of lectures, discussions, and activities to support student success. ·          Use Xavier’s campus-wide academic program, Canvas, to provide course information and maintain an electronic record of student’s progress. ·          Working cooperatively with members of the department. To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University’s website.   Please note: This adjunct faculty pool will end on May 31, 2027 . If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new adjunct pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is an equal opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Adjunct-Faculty---College-of-Health---Human-Sciences_JR100496": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - College of Health & Human Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Adjunct Faculty - College of Health & Human Sciences ‌ Xavier University is seeking qualified candidates to join our pool of potential adjunct faculty for the 2026-2027 academic year. This posting is intended to collect applications for part-time, non-tenure-track position for an Adjunct Instructor in the College of Health & Human Sciences. Candidates must be dedicated to graduate or undergraduate teaching and demonstrate excellence in their field.  The successful candidate will contribute to our commitment to excellence in teaching and student engagement. Applications will be accepted on a continuous basis , and candidates may be contacted as teaching needs arise. Adjunct faculty contracts are issued on a semester-by-semester basis, depending on departmental needs and student enrollment. Minimum Qualifications: ·       Depending on the courses assigned, candidates may qualify with a master’s degree in a related field accompanied by significant professional experience or a relevant graduate degree. ·       Demonstrated ability to teach at the college level. Duties include: ·       Teach assigned course(s). ·       Effective planning and preparation of lectures, discussions, and activities to support student success. ·       Use Xavier’s campus-wide academic program, Canvas, to provide course information and maintain an electronic record of student’s progress. ·       Working cooperatively with members of the department. To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University’s website.  Please note: This adjunct faculty pool will end on May 31 , 2027 . If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new adjunct pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is an equal opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
